Closes #454. Closes #473.

RDFLib reassignment queries now compile through a typed Rust algebra route into the shared evaluator. Graph, processor, Dataset, ConjunctiveGraph and shadow consumers preserve context and initial bindings through nested EXISTS, projection, OPTIONAL, MINUS, grouping and ordered delivery. Single-graph GRAPH operations return the typed dataset-required error.

Python query rows provide checked length, signed positional indexing and a lazy owning iterator. Duplicate labels retain every positional cell and the compatibility route's final-label lookup. Iterators retain their result owner through exhaustion and caller lifetimes.

Integration preserves dated SHACL admission: contextual application has its own typed reason. Project and worker checkpoint paths use the shared bulk and replay homes. No new runtime dependency, semantic feature, second parser or evaluator is introduced. Documentation and Chinese translations describe the shipped interfaces.

